message: "If you use or refer to this research prototype, please cite this software record."
title: "KHALAF-MUB-001-4B: An Arabic Dialect Language Model and Dataset for an Al-Mubarraz Colloquial Variety"
type: software
version: "v0.4.1"
date-released: 2026-11-24
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24505487
authors:
  - family-names: Almomen
    given-names: Yasmin
repository-code: "https://github.com/yaass24/KHALAF-MUB-001-4B"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24505487"
abstract: >-
  KHALAF is an exploratory Arabic dialect-to-Modern Standard Arabic model
  adapted from Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 using QLoRA and 2,500 training
  pairs. It documents one contributor-centered colloquial speech variety
  used in Al-Mubarraz city, Al-Ahsa Governorate, Saudi Arabia. The project
  emphasizes everyday speaking patterns, phrasing, and morphology and
  does not claim to represent all varieties spoken in Al-Mubarraz.
  Training data combine human-authored or reviewed examples and
  AI-assisted synthetic expansions with varied review depth; errors may
  remain. The full Zenodo v0.4.1 archive contains the dataset, lexicon,
  LoRA adapter, inference notebook, and documentation. GitHub hosts code
  and documentation but not the full downloadable archive.
keywords:
  - Arabic natural language processing
  - Al-Mubarraz
  - Al-Ahsa
  - dialect-to-MSA
  - low-resource languages
  - QLoRA
  - linguistic heritage
